  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Speed into the pass and finish",
  "description": "Two groups, A on the left and B on the right, at the centre line. Put out a turning cone and a finishing cone on each side of the attacking half, and a goalkeeper in goal. The coach stands at the centre circle with the balls.\n\nA sets off at full speed without a ball, rounds the turning cone and gets a pass from the coach. A carries the ball past the finishing cone into the middle and shoots. As soon as A has the pass, B starts the same way from the other side. After the shot the player joins the other group and returns the ball to the coach.\n\nProgression: the coach passes harder or further in front of the player, or a defender starts from the centre line and tries to disrupt. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Full speed into the reception – don't slow down to take the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Both hands on the stick when carrying the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Show the coach with your stick where you want the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Look up at the goalkeeper before you shoot."
    }
  ],
